{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-79747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a rectangular solid, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the surface area $S$ of the rectangular solid if the base is a square with the side of $a=3$ and the height is $h=7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The surface area of the given rectangular solid is $S=2{a}^{2}+4ah.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(a,h) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂S}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =(4a+4h)\\,\\text{d}a+4a\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=3$ and $h=7,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(3,7) & =(4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 7)\\,\\text{d}a+4\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =40\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64ebbe4c5c3339e384772d524cb74d16e51e6558d9210f91128095b076ca4c95"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,\\text{d}a+24\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "17\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "20\\,\\text{d}a+24\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "40\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h"] ["math" "40\\,\\text{d}a+48\\,\\text{d}h"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79747" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "40\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.12)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},0),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡0\\,\\text{d}x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{cos}⁡0\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3}+Δx,0+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+\\frac{1}{2}\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.12)=f(1,0.12),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(1,0.12).$\n\nMoving from $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},0)$ to $(1,0.12),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1-\\frac{\\pi }{3}, \\\\ Δy & =0.12-0=0.12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\cdot (1-\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (0.12) \\\\  & ≈0+0.5\\cdot 0.12 \\\\  & ≈0.06.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.06.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,0.12) & ≈f(\\frac{\\pi }{3},0)+0.06 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.12) & ≈\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+0.06 \\\\  & ≈0+0.06 \\\\  & ≈0.06.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64ebbe4c5c3339e384772d524cb74d16e51e6558d9210f91128095b076ca4c95"} {"question" "q-79836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.058"] ["math" "0.060"] ["math" "0.062"] ["math" "0.064"] ["math" "0.066"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.060"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $(1.06)^{4.1}$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{y}$ at the point $(1,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =y{x}^{y-1}\\,\\text{d}x+{x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(1,4),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =4\\cdot {1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{1}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\,\\text{d}x+0\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(1+Δx,4+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈4\\,Δx+0\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n(1.06)^{4.1}=f(1.06,4.1),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(1.06,4.1).$\n\nMoving from $(1,4)$ to $(1.06,4.1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1.06-1=0.06, \\\\ Δy & =4.1-4=0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈4\\cdot (0.06)+0\\cdot (0.1) \\\\  & ≈0.24+0 \\\\  & ≈0.24\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.24.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.06,4.1) & ≈f(1,4)+0.24 \\\\ (1.06)^{4.1} & ≈{1}^{4}+0.24 \\\\  & ≈1+0.24 \\\\  & ≈1.24\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64ebbe4c5c3339e384772d524cb74d16e51e6558d9210f91128095b076ca4c95"} {"question" "q-79876" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79876" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.22"] ["math" "1.24"] ["math" "1.26"] ["math" "1.28"] ["math" "1.30"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-79876" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({z}^{3}-y),$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y,z)$ from $(2,-3,1)$ to $(1,-2,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2x\\,\\text{d}x-(\\frac{4}{{z}^{3}-y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{12{z}^{2}}{{z}^{3}-y})\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(2,-3,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(2,-3,1) & =(2\\cdot 2)\\,\\text{d}x-(\\frac{4}{{1}^{3}-(-3)})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{12\\cdot {1}^{2}}{{1}^{3}-(-3)})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =4\\,\\text{d}x-\\,\\text{d}y+3\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(2+Δx,-3+Δy,1+Δz),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈4\\,Δx-\\,Δy+3\\,Δz.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(2,-3,1)$ to $(1,-2,2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1-2=-1, \\\\ Δy & =-2-(-3)=1 \\\\ Δz & =2-1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈4\\,Δx-1\\,Δy+3\\,Δz \\\\  & ≈4\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ≈-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y,z)$ decreases by approximately $-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64ebbe4c5c3339e384772d524cb74d16e51e6558d9210f91128095b076ca4c95"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-168150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a rectangular solid, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ of the rectangular solid if the lengths of the sides are $a=6,$ $b=3,$ and $c=8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-168150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The volume of the rectangular solid is $V=abc.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(a,b,c) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂V}{∂b})\\,\\text{d}b+(\\frac{∂V}{∂c})\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =bc\\,\\text{d}a+ac\\,\\text{d}b+ab\\,\\text{d}c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=6,$ $b=3,$ and $c=8,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(6,3,8) & =3\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}a+6\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}b+6\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}c \\\\  & =24\\,\\text{d}a+48\\,\\text{d}b+18\\,\\text{d}c.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-168150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64ebbe4c5c3339e384772d524cb74d16e51e6558d9210f91128095b076ca4c95"} {"question" "q-168150" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-168150" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12\\,\\text{d}a+24\\,\\text{d}b+9\\,\\text{d}c"] ["math" "18\\,\\text{d}a+24\\,\\text{d}b+48\\,\\text{d}c"] ["math" "24\\,\\text{d}a+48\\,\\text{d}b+18\\,\\text{d}c"] ["math" "36\\,\\text{d}a+9\\,\\text{d}b+64\\,\\text{d}c"] ["math" "6\\,\\text{d}a+3\\,\\text{d}b+9\\,\\text{d}c"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "bec3894082ff6c8e40deb17c5606b594cc1334359a941d50b6f4c3ddc0feaa9e"} {"question" "q-168150" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.t